🤖 Advanced Python Chatbot

📌 About the Project

Advanced Python Chatbot is a rule-based conversational program developed using Python. It interacts with users, provides predefined responses, performs basic mathematical calculations, and stores chat history in a JSON file.

This project was created as part of the CodeAlpha Python Programming Internship.

✨ Features

- Interactive chatbot conversation
- Smart keyword-based responses
- Random greetings and jokes
- Current date and time
- Basic calculator with safe expression evaluation
- Chat history storage using JSON
- View previous conversations
- Clear chat history
- Input validation and error handling
- Help menu and exit commands

🛠️ Technologies Used

- Python 3
- Random module
- Datetime module
- JSON module
- AST module
- OS module

▶️ How to Run

1. Install Python 3 or open Pydroid 3 on Android.
2. Open the "advanced_chatbot.py" file.
3. Run the program.
4. Type "help" to view available commands.
5. Enter your message and interact with the chatbot.

💬 Available Commands

- "hello" — Get a greeting
- "how are you" — Ask how the bot is doing
- "your name" — Ask the chatbot's name
- "time" — Display the current time
- "date" — Display today's date
- "joke" — Get a random joke
- "motivation" — Receive a motivational message
- "study" — Get a study tip
- "calculate: 25 * 4" — Perform a calculation
- "history" — View saved conversations
- "clear history" — Clear saved conversations
- "help" — Display available commands
- "bye" — Exit the chatbot

📁 Project Files

- "advanced_chatbot.py" — Main Python program
- "chat_history.json" — Stores chat history automatically when the chatbot runs

🎯 Learning Outcomes

This project demonstrates the use of Python functions, dictionaries, loops, conditional statements, exception handling, JSON file handling, and safe expression evaluation.

